{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Like gluttons</b> — the reverse of והלמה סיסרא (and she struck Sisera), and it is a verb with an object, like התגלחו את נזרו (they shaved their consecration). The meaning: like strikers, so are the words of the grumbler, and he is the talebearer, as in לכו ונכהו בלשון (come and let us strike him with the tongue), and these are words." "<b>Belly</b> — an allusion to the heart."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The lemma translated as 'gluttons' (כמתלהמים) reflects Ibn Ezra's parsing of the word as related to striking/blows; the citation והלמה is from Judges 5:26, and לכו ונכהו בלשון from Jeremiah 18:18."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:56.932861911Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}